</div><noscript><p class="note-js">This calculator needs JavaScript. Turn it on, or call (844) 537-1427 and we’ll run the numbers with you.</p></noscript>
<p class="hint">For planning only. Results depend on what you enter and on your policy, and aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why the cause decides the coverage</h2>
<p>A typical Ohio homeowners policy treats basement water in very different ways depending on the source:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Sudden pipe or appliance discharge</strong> is usually covered under the main policy, subject to the deductible and the policy’s conditions.</li>
<li><strong>Sewer or drain backup and sump pump failure</strong> are usually excluded unless you bought a water backup endorsement — and that endorsement normally has its own limit, often $5,000 to $25,000.</li>
<li><strong>Surface water and river flooding</strong> are excluded from homeowners policies; that’s what NFIP or private flood insurance is for, and flood policies limit basement coverage.</li>
<li><strong>Long-term seepage</strong> is commonly excluded as wear, maintenance or repeated leakage.</li></ul>
<h2>What the calculator assumes</h2>
<p>It applies the deductible once, caps a backup loss at the endorsement limit, and treats flood and seepage as outside the homeowners policy. For flood it applies the limit you enter, but real flood policies restrict which basement items are covered, so the flood result is optimistic. Policies differ; your endorsement may cover the deductible differently or include mitigation in the limit.</p>
<h2>Where appraisal fits</h2>
<p>Appraisal can settle how much a covered basement loss costs, but not which cause applies. If the insurer says the water was flood rather than backup, that’s a coverage question. Read more on our <a href="/appraisal-practice/water-damage-appraisal/">water damage appraisal</a> page.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Illustrative only</b>Default numbers are examples. Check your declarations page for the actual endorsement limit.</div>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is a sump pump failure the same as sewer backup?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many endorsements group them together as water that backs up through drains or overflows from a sump. Read the endorsement title and wording on your own policy.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does the endorsement limit include water extraction?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Often yes — dry-out and cleanup usually come out of the same limit as repairs, which is why small limits run out fast in finished basements.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can appraisal raise my backup sublimit?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. Appraisal sets the amount of loss, but the policy limit still caps the payment. It can matter when the true loss is disputed and still under the limit.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-workbench/claim-gap-fee-estimator/"><small>Estimator</small><span>Claim Gap &amp; Fee Estimator</span><svg class="ar" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-workbench/rcv-acv-holdback-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>RCV/ACV Holdback Calculator</span><svg class="ar" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-workbench/roof-area-pitch-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Roof Area &amp; Pitch Calculator</span><svg class="ar" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><aside c